      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nPR #52228 provides support adaptive verification without a confidence head and this PR enable it for XPU path. We identified perf gap caused by FA kernel and can be addressed by PR [647](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-xpu-kernels/pull/647). With these 2 PRs, we got below bench results:\n\n## Performance Summary\n\nBenchmarked Muse-Glimmer-30B + DFlash2 on **8 Intel Arc Pro B60 GPUs (TP8)**,\ncomparing adaptive verification enabled/disabled at K=3/5/7.\n\nServer launch:\n```\nADAPTIVE=true\n\n\"${VLLM[@]}\" serve \"$MODEL\" \\\n  --served-model-name \"$MODEL\" --port 8000 \\\n  --tokenizer-mode deepseek_v4 --trust-remote-code \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\\n  --max-model-len 8192 --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 \\\n  --max-num-seqs 128 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.88 \\\n  --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"FULL_DECODE_ONLY\"}' \\\n  --no-enable-prefix-caching \\\n  --speculative-config \"{\n    \\\"method\\\":\\\"dflash\\\",\n    \\\"model\\\":\\\"z-lab/Muse-Glimmer-30B-DFlash2\\\",\n    \\\"attention_backend\\\":\\\"FLASH_ATTN\\\",\n    \\\"num_speculative_tokens\\\":${K},\n    \\\"draft_sample_method\\\":\\\"probabilistic\\\",\n    \\\"enable_adaptive_verification\\\":${ADAPTIVE}\n  }\"\n```\n\nOutput throughput change with adaptive verification enabled, relative to\ndisabled at the same K:\n\n| Workload | K3 | K5 | K7 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SPEED, high entropy, BS24 | -2.59% | +5.40% | +6.25% |\n| SPEED, low entropy, BS24 | -4.99% | +3.81% | +2.21% |\n| Sonnet, BS32 | -3.18% | +11.10% | +11.70% |\n\n- **SPEED:** 12 configurations, 512 requests/configuration, 512 output\n  tokens/request. Adaptive verification improves K5/K7 throughput, while K3\n  without adaptive remains the fastest measured configuration.\n- **Sonnet:** 6 configurations, 96 requests/configuration, 2048 output\n  tokens/request. K5 + adaptive achieves the highest throughput\n  (**468.55 tok/s**), 2.80% above K3 without adaptive. Mean E2E latency decreases\n  by **8.17% at K5** and **10.98% at K7** versus their respective disabled controls.\n- All **6,720 requests succeeded**, with zero failures.\n\n\n",
